%description:

Tcp.accEcnOptionPolicy:linux-duplicate -- a CE-marked duplicate that ends at RCV.NXT counts in the ACE field.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "AccECN: when the option goes out and which fields it has. "rfc": the
recommended scheme of RFC 9768 section 3.2.3.3 ...; "linux": as Linux tcp_ecn_option=2: on each
segment, kind 174 with each field that fits".

The classes: rfc (the default) and linux (the value of LinuxTcp), with the facets kind and
duplicate. The code:
TcpConnection::writeHeaderOptions() puts the option of order 0 (kind 172: EE0B, ECEB, EE1B) on
the SYN-ACK with "rfc", and the option of order 1 (kind 174: EE1B, ECEB, EE0B) with "linux";
after the handshake, TcpConnection::getAccEcnOptionFields() decides when the option goes out.
With "linux", TcpConnection::processSegment1stThru8th() counts a duplicate segment that ends at
RCV.NXT in the AccECN counters, as Linux tests the acceptability against the left edge of the
window that it advertised last. This test separates "linux" from "rfc".

Host under test: host2, an AccECN server (tcpEcnMode "accecn-passive"; host1 "accecn":
preconditions); host1 sends 1448 bytes, of which the first segment carries 1436, because the
AccECN option on the first data segment takes 12 bytes. The tap sends a copy of that segment 1
ms later,
and marks only the copy CE. No packet was CE-marked before, so the ACE field holds 5 (RFC 9768
section 3.2.2.1). Observation: level 1, the ACK of host2 after the copy has the ACE field 6:
AE 1, CWR 1, ECE 0.

%# parameter: Tcp.accEcnOptionPolicy
%# class: linux-duplicate
%# value: "linux"
%# key: *.host2.tcp.accEcnOptionPolicy
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAccEcnOptionPolicyLinuxDuplicate")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).duplicate(0.001)
                     .describe("the data segment of host1: a copy 1 ms later"))
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").copiesOnly().set("ipv4.ecn", "3")
                     .describe("the copy: CE-marked"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the data segment at host2")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the CE-marked copy at host2")
             .within(0.01))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo > {isn} + 1")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.aeBit == true && tcp.cwrBit == true && tcp.eceBit == false")
             .describe("the ACK of host2 after the copy")
             .within(0.01));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAccEcnOptionPolicyLinuxDuplicate compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.accEcnOptionPolicy = "linux"    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"
*.host2.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn-passive"
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 1448B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAccEcnOptionPolicyLinuxDuplicate: PASS
